1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,904
Smart contracts run for years, and there is no tail -f for a live protocol.

2
00:00:04,904 --> 00:00:11,115
When something breaks, you usually hear about it on Telegram, an hour after the funds are gone.

3
00:00:11,115 --> 00:00:15,953
Argus turns Splunk into a security operations center for cross-chain DeFi.

4
00:00:15,953 --> 00:00:19,362
This is Argus monitoring LayerZero, live in Splunk.

5
00:00:19,362 --> 00:00:25,980
Every on-chain transaction, event, source file, and audit report becomes a typed Splunk sourcetype.

6
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:31,462
Millions of transactions indexed across fifteen in-scope contracts on five chains.

7
00:00:31,462 --> 00:00:32,856
Detection is pure SPL.

8
00:00:32,856 --> 00:00:39,384
Per-contract z-score outliers on transfer value and decoded token amount, with no hardcoded thresholds.

9
00:00:39,384 --> 00:00:42,109
The contract teaches Splunk what is normal.

10
00:00:42,109 --> 00:00:47,306
And Argus is honest: it separates real anomalies from ordinary protocol lifecycle.

11
00:00:47,306 --> 00:00:53,580
We found and disabled a rule that was flagging normal LayerZero message delivery as replay attacks.

12
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:55,799
A clean baseline beats crying wolf.

13
00:00:55,799 --> 00:01:00,923
An AI agent runs inside the Splunk app itself, as a modular input on the Python SDK.

14
00:01:00,923 --> 00:01:07,694
It triages each finding in-process and writes its verdict back as a Splunk event, deduplicated in the KV store.

15
00:01:07,694 --> 00:01:14,831
Here it surfaced nine value-manipulation candidates on Puffer pufETH and Ethena USDe, each with a recommended action.

16
00:01:14,831 --> 00:01:18,397
High-severity candidates become proof-of-concept triggers.

17
00:01:18,397 --> 00:01:27,868
An external Anvil mainnet fork runs a Foundry exploit test, and Argus marks a finding confirmed only when the test's own assertions reproduce the exploit.

18
00:01:27,868 --> 00:01:31,127
Never on a guess, and never with a fabricated number.

19
00:01:31,127 --> 00:01:32,881
Everything runs on Splunk.

20
00:01:32,881 --> 00:01:38,887
Splunk does the pattern work, holds the state, and runs the agent, with zero external AI.

21
00:01:38,887 --> 00:01:42,126
Argus is what using Splunk correctly looks like.

22
00:01:42,126 --> 00:01:47,187
Open source, protocol-agnostic, built for the Splunk Agentic Ops Hackathon.

